"9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1f551e483c07e63c6d7b434f87110bb9354c33b645a026f26459e15efc8069f"} {"question" "q-108902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "14"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-39361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=-3$, the $5$th term ${a}_{5}=5$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=192.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-39361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{5}-{a}_{1}}{5-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-(-3)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=-3$, $d=2$, and ${S}_{N}=192$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 192 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(-3)+(N-1)(2)) \\\\ 192 & =\\frac{N}{2}(-6+2N-2) \\\\ 192 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2N-8) \\\\ 192 & =N(N-4) \\\\ 192 & ={N}^{2}-4N \\\\ {N}^{2}-4N-192 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-192)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{784}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 28}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=16$ or $N=-12.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=16$ terms." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-39361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1f551e483c07e63c6d7b434f87110bb9354c33b645a026f26459e15efc8069f"} {"question" "q-39361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-39361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "19"] ["math" "20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-39361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=4$, the $8$th term ${a}_{8}=60$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=1600.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{8}-{a}_{1}}{8-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-4}{8-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{7} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=4$, $d=8$, and ${S}_{N}=1600$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 1600 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 4+(N-1)\\cdot 8) \\\\ 1600 & =\\frac{N}{2}(8+8N-8) \\\\ 1600 & =\\frac{N}{2}(8N) \\\\ 1600 & =4{N}^{2} \\\\ 400 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1f551e483c07e63c6d7b434f87110bb9354c33b645a026f26459e15efc8069f"} {"question" "q-5446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "23"] ["math" "29"] ["math" "31"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=-1$ the $6$th term ${a}_{6}=1.5,$ and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=6.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{6}-{a}_{1}}{6-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5-(-1)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.5}{5} \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=-1$, $d=0.5$, and ${S}_{N}=6$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 6 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot (-1)+(N-1)\\cdot 0.5) \\\\ 12 & =N(-2+0.5N-0.5) \\\\ 12 & =N(0.5N-2.5) \\\\ 12 & =0.5{N}^{2}-2.5N \\\\ 24 & ={N}^{2}-5N\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the above equation, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{N}^{2}-5N-24 & =0 \\\\ (N-8)(N+3) & =0 \\\\ N & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive solution because $N$ can't be negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1f551e483c07e63c6d7b434f87110bb9354c33b645a026f26459e15efc8069f"} {"question" "q-108930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=-3,$ the second term is ${a}_{2}=0,$ and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=27.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=-3,$ $d=3,$ and ${S}_{N}=27$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 27 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(-3)+(N-1)(3)) \\\\ 54 & =N(-6+3N-3) \\\\ 54 & =N(3N-9) \\\\ 54 & =3{N}^{2}-9N\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the above equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{N}^{2}-9N-54 & =0 \\\\ {N}^{2}-3N-18 & =0 \\\\ (N-6)(N+3) & =0 \\\\ N & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive solution because $N$ can't be negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1f551e483c07e63c6d7b434f87110bb9354c33b645a026f26459e15efc8069f"} {"question" "q-108928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-108928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=12$, the second term is ${a}_{2}=36$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=588.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =36-12 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=12$, $d=24$, and ${S}_{N}=588$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(12)+(N-1)(24)) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(24+24N-24) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(24N) \\\\ 588 & =12{N}^{2} \\\\ 49 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1f551e483c07e63c6d7b434f87110bb9354c33b645a026f26459e15efc8069f"} {"question" "q-5492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "q-5492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/state.json" "file_sha256" "9df0caecd4385f699e67f169d19a11e66337bb6fdba2c06ac6fe80a4f3b1caf4"} {"question" "e-4205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The first term of an arithmetic series is $a_1=2,$ the common difference is $d=4,$ and the sum of the series is $S_N=200.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/example-4205.json" "file_sha256" "1ffa622ce9d2df5042c23399f29d3e6421122aa07acc21ecbb5f49334e507f8b"} {"question" "e-4205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the number of terms, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac N 2 \\big(2a_1 + (N-1) d \\big)\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a_1=2,$ $d=4,$ and $S_N=200$ into the above and solve for $N,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 200 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 2+(N-1)\\cdot 4) \\\\ 200 & =\\frac{N}{2}(4+4N-4) \\\\ 200 & =\\frac{N}{2}(4N) \\\\ 200 & =2{N}^{2} \\\\ 100 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have taken the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/example-4205.json" "file_sha256" "1ffa622ce9d2df5042c23399f29d3e6421122aa07acc21ecbb5f49334e507f8b"} {"question" "e-4203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n5+7+9+\\cdots = 140\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/example-4203.json" "file_sha256" "74e03d3058ca74dcfe5748f0e4c771ded80f50354f0307ad6762d755b8452de6"} {"question" "e-4203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\nS_{N} = \\dfrac{N}{2} \\big( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\big)\n$$\n\nWe are given the sum $S_N = 140,$ and the first term $a_1=5.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 140 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(5)+(N-1)(2)) \\\\ 140 & =\\frac{N}{2}(10+2N-2) \\\\ 140 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2N+8) \\\\ 140 & ={N}^{2}+4N \\\\ 0 & ={N}^{2}+4N-140.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{{4}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-140)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{576}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 24}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $N=10$ or $N=-14.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=10$ terms." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/example-4203.json" "file_sha256" "74e03d3058ca74dcfe5748f0e4c771ded80f50354f0307ad6762d755b8452de6"} {"question" "e-4204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "An arithmetic series has the $5$th term $a_{5}=14,$ the $7$th term $a_{7}=19,$ and the sum of the series is $S_N=850.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/example-4204.json" "file_sha256" "7752db9950617cf435553fd2e57155f4f9dd4f8c99194d13a11c7cfdac830193"} {"question" "e-4204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac N 2 \\big( 2a_1 + (N-1) d \\big)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{7}-{a}_{5}}{7-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{19-14}{7-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that $a_{5}=14.$ We can compute $a_1$ using the formula for the $n$th term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}+(5-1)\\cdot 2.5 \\\\ 14 & ={a}_{1}+4\\cdot 2.5 \\\\ 14 & ={a}_{1}+10 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, substituting $a_1=4,$ $d=2.5,$ and $S_N=850$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 850 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(4)+(N-1)(2.5)) \\\\ 850 & =\\frac{N}{2}(8+2.5N-2.5) \\\\ 850\\cdot 2 & =N(5.5+2.5N) \\\\ 1700 & =2.5{N}^{2}+5.5N \\\\ 2.5{N}^{2}+5.5N-1\\,700 & =0 \\\\ 5{N}^{2}+11N-3\\,400 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-(11)\\pm \\sqrt{(-11)^{2}-4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-3400)}}{2\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11\\pm \\sqrt{68\\,121}}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11\\pm 261}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $N=25$ or $N=-27.2.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be a positive integer.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=25$ terms." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043389/example-4204.json" "file_sha256" "7752db9950617cf435553fd2e57155f4f9dd4f8c99194d13a11c7cfdac830193"}] "usage" {"q-5446" [] "e-4204" [] "e-4205" [] "e-4203" []} "basis" 1609 "retractions" [[17592186079035 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nAn arithmetic series has the first term $a_{1} = 4$, the $8$th term $a_{8} = 60$, and the sum of the series is $S_{N} = 1600$. Find the number of terms $N$ in the series."] [17592186078222 :question/problem "The first term of an arithmetic series is $a_1=2$, the common difference is $d=4$, and the sum of the series is $S_N=200$. Find the number of terms $N$ in the series."] [17592186078222 :question/worked-solution "To find the number of terms, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac N 2 \\big(2a_1 + (N-1) d \\big)\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a_1=2$, $d=4$, and $S_N=200$ into the above and solve for $N$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= \\frac{N}{2}(2a_{1} + (N - 1)d) \\\\\n200 &= \\frac{N}{2}(2 \\cdot 2 + (N - 1) \\cdot 4) \\\\\n200 &= \\frac{N}{2}(4 + 4N - 4) \\\\\n200 &= \\frac{N}{2}(4N) \\\\\n200 &= 2N^{2} \\\\\n100 &= N^{2} \\\\\nN &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have taken the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative."] [17592186078220 :question/problem "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series:\n$5+7+9+\\cdots = 140$"] [17592186078220 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\nS_{N} = \\dfrac{N}{2} \\big(2a_1+(N-1)d \\big)\n$$\n\nWe are given the sum $S_N = 140$, and the first term $a_1=5$. Our goal is to find $N$, the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= a_{2} - a_{1} \\\\\n&= 7 - 5 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= \\frac{N}{2}(2a_{1} + (N - 1)d) \\\\\n140 &= \\frac{N}{2}(2(5) + (N - 1)(2)) \\\\\n140 &= \\frac{N}{2}(10 + 2N - 2) \\\\\n140 &= \\frac{N}{2}(2N + 8) \\\\\n140 &= N^{2} + 4N \\\\\n0 &= N^{2} + 4N - 140\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN &= (-4 ± \\sqrt{4^{2} - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-140)})/(2 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-4 ± \\sqrt{576}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-4 ± 24}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $N=10$ or $N=-14$. We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=10$ terms."] [17592186078221 :question/problem "An arithmetic series has the $5$th term $a_{5}=14$, the $7$th term $a_{7}=19$, and the sum of the series is $S_N=850$. Find the number of terms $N$ in the series."] [17592186078221 :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac N 2 \\big(2a_1 + (N-1) d \\big)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= \\frac{a_{7} - a_{5}}{7 - 5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{19 - 14}{7 - 5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{2} \\\\\n&= 2.5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that $a_{5}=14$. We can compute $a_1$ using the formula for the $n$th term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} + (n - 1)d \\\\\na_{5} &= a_{1} + (5 - 1) \\cdot 2.5 \\\\\n14 &= a_{1} + 4 \\cdot 2.5 \\\\\n14 &= a_{1} + 10 \\\\\na_{1} &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $a_1=4$, $d=2.5$, and $S_N=850$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= \\frac{N}{2}(2a_{1} + (N - 1)d) \\\\\n850 &= \\frac{N}{2}(2(4) + (N - 1)(2.5)) \\\\\n850 &= \\frac{N}{2}(8 + 2.5N - 2.5) \\\\\n850 \\cdot 2 &= N(5.5 + 2.5N) \\\\\n1700 &= 2.5N^{2} + 5.5N \\\\\n2.5N^{2} + 5.5N - 1700 &= 0 \\\\\n5N^{2} + 11N - 3400 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN &= (- (11) ± \\sqrt{(-11)^{2} - 4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot (-3400)})/(2 \\cdot 5) \\\\\n&= \\frac{-11 ± \\sqrt{68121}}{10} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-11 ± 261}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $N=25$ or $N=-27.2$. We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be a positive integer.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=25$ terms."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186077422 17592186077423 17592186077424 17592186077425 17592186077426] "immutable_fields" [[17592186077421 :answer-field/correct] [17592186077421 :answer-field/id] [1759